<div id="S2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S2.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is strongly graded, Dade’s Theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 1.5.1]</cite> (see also
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Theorem 3.1.1]</cite>), guarantees that the functors <math id="S2.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-)_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-)_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\otimes_{R_{0}}-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\otimes_{R_{0}}-</annotation></semantics></math> form mutually inverse equivalences of categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Note that in general <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-)_{0}:R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-)_{0}:R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not induce a functor <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-)_{0}:R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-)_{0}:R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is strongly graded if and only if <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>, if and only if <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}{\bf gr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠𝐫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}{\bf gr}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\text{-}{\bf mod}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦𝐨𝐝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\text{-}{\bf mod}</annotation></semantics></math>, both under the functors (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2. Graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2. Graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>). Here <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}{\bf gr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠𝐫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}{\bf gr}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the category of graded finitely generated <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules and <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\text{-}{\bf mod}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦𝐨𝐝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\text{-}{\bf mod}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of finitely generated <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras and let <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A\rightarrow R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A\rightarrow R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j:A\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j:A\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded algebra monomorphisms (so we identify <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> as a graded subring of <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>). The coproduct <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R*_{A}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R*_{A}S</annotation></semantics></math> can be given a natural <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-grading, so that this coproduct is indeed the pushout for the graded maps <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3. </span>Matrix form of graded homomorphisms</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be an abelian group, <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> a <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded commutative ring with identity and <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> a <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A graded <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module is called a <span id="S2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">graded free</span> module, if it is a free module with homogeneous basis. Clearly a graded free module is a free module. A graded free <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module can be presented as <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\gamma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A graded <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">graded projective</span> module if <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is a projective <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. One can check that <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is graded projective if and only if the functor <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(P,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(P,-)</annotation></semantics></math> is an exact functor in the category <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is graded isomorphic to a direct summand of a graded free <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Proposition 1.2.15]</cite>). So a module is graded projective module if and only if it is graded and projective. This is not the case for graded free module. A module could be graded and free, but not graded free (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, § 1.2.4]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, if <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded finitely generated projective <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module, then there is a graded finitely generated projective <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\bigoplus Q\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>gr</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\bigoplus Q\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{n}(\overline{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{n}(\overline{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{1},\cdots,\alpha_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{1},\cdots,\alpha_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">One observes that <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\operatorname{Hom}}_{R}(R(\delta_{j}),R(\delta_{i}))\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}R(\delta_{i}-\delta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>gr</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\operatorname{Hom}}_{R}(R(\delta_{j}),R(\delta_{i}))\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}R(\delta_{i}-\delta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> as graded <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. Hence we have the following isomorphisms:</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))\\
&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(R(\alpha_{i}),R(\beta_{j}))\\
&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))\\
&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(R(\alpha_{i}),R(\beta_{j}))\\
&amp;\cong\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
