<div id="S2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For a <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{j})_{j\in J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{j})_{j\in J}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\beta_{j}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\beta_{j}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, set</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]:={\begin{pmatrix}R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}\end{pmatrix}}_{i\in I,j\in J}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]:={\begin{pmatrix}R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}\end{pmatrix}}_{i\in I,j\in J},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where for each <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, only a finite number of entries in <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> are non-zero. Thus <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math> consists of matrices with the <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math>-entry in <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with a finite number of non-zero elements in each row. One observes that <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the set <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i}),\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math> as follows: Suppose that <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module homomorphism. Then for each <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(1_{i})=(u_{ij})_{j\in J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(1_{i})=(u_{ij})_{j\in J}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the element of <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> whose <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component is <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and whose other components are zero (note that <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(1_{i})=-\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(1_{i})=-\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{ij}\in R(\beta_{j})_{-\alpha_{i}}=R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{ij}\in R(\beta_{j})_{-\alpha_{i}}=R_{\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> are all zero except for a finite number of <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the graded homomorphism <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by multiplying the matrix <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\in\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\in\mathbb{M}_{I\times J}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math> from the right. Suppose that <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v:\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{k\in K}R(\gamma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v:\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{k\in K}R(\gamma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by multiplying the matrix <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}\in\mathbb{M}_{J\times K}(R)[\overline{\beta}][\overline{\gamma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}\in\mathbb{M}_{J\times K}(R)[\overline{\beta}][\overline{\gamma}]</annotation></semantics></math> from the right. Then the composition <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\circ u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\circ u</annotation></semantics></math> is given by multiplying the matrix <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\cdot(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\cdot(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}</annotation></semantics></math> from the right. Here,</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\cdot(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u_{ij})_{i\in I,j\in J}\cdot(v_{jk})_{j\in J,k\in K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">is the multiplication of matrices. Notice that the matrix representation of the composition of functions <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\circ u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\circ u</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by swapping the orders (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The above notion of <em id="S2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mixed-shift</em> was developed for graded right <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, §1.3.4]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In fact, any element in <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i\in I}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> in the last equation of (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) can be written as <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j}-\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a row vector indexed by <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S2.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> having finitely many non-zero entries for each <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For a <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{1},\cdots,\alpha_{m})\in\Gamma^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{1},\cdots,\alpha_{m})\in\Gamma^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{1},\cdots,\beta_{n})\in\Gamma^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{1},\cdots,\beta_{n})\in\Gamma^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.6</span></a>) takes the form</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]={\begin{pmatrix}R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{1}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{1}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{1}}\\
R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{2}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{2}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{2}}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{m}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{m}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{m}}\\
\end{pmatrix}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]={\begin{pmatrix}R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{1}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{1}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{1}}\\
R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{2}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{2}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{2}}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
R_{\beta_{1}-\alpha_{m}}&amp;R_{\beta_{2}-\alpha_{m}}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{\beta_{n}-\alpha_{m}}\\
\end{pmatrix}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the set <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(R^{m}(\overline{\alpha}),R^{n}(\overline{\beta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Hom}_{R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}}(R^{m}(\overline{\alpha}),R^{n}(\overline{\beta}))</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n</annotation></semantics></math>, we simply write <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)[\overline{\alpha}][\overline{\beta}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) we have the graded matrix ring
<math id="S2.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{End}_{R}(R^{n}(\overline{\alpha}))\cong\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{j}-\alpha_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>End</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{End}_{R}(R^{n}(\overline{\alpha}))\cong\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\alpha_{j}-\alpha_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)(\overline{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)(\overline{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely</p>
