</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)(\overline{\alpha})_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)(\overline{\alpha})_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-homogeneous elements, are the
<math id="S2.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math>-matrices over <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> with the degree shifted (suspended) as follows</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
