<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> the free <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra generated by the set <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> the two-sided ideal of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the set</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big\{rp_{\gamma}+sp_{\gamma}-(r+s)p_{\gamma}\mid r,s\in R_{\delta};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma\big\}\bigcup\big\{rp_{\gamma}sp_{\delta}-rs_{\gamma-\delta}p_{\delta}\mid r,s\in R^{h};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.497em">;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.497em">;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\{rp_{\gamma}+sp_{\gamma}-(r+s)p_{\gamma}\mid r,s\in R_{\delta};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma\big\}\bigcup\big\{rp_{\gamma}sp_{\delta}-rs_{\gamma-\delta}p_{\delta}\mid r,s\in R^{h};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly the <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta:F\to R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta:F\to R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> defined by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> induces a <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}:F/I\to R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}:F/I\to R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subseteq\ker(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subseteq\ker(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>). Since the elements <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},\gamma\in\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> generate the <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the homomorphism <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. It remains to show that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. Suppose that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in F/I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in F/I</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero. Clearly we can write <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=r_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}+\dots+r_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=r_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}+\dots+r_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\in R^{h}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\in R^{h}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> set <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\gamma):=\{1\leq i\leq n\mid\gamma_{i}=\gamma\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\gamma):=\{1\leq i\leq n\mid\gamma_{i}=\gamma\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We may assume that</span></p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(r_{i})\neq\deg(r_{j}),\text{ for any }\gamma\in\Gamma\text{ and }i\neq j\in J(\gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> for any </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(r_{i})\neq\deg(r_{j}),\text{ for any }\gamma\in\Gamma\text{ and }i\neq j\in J(\gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=\bar{\theta}(x)=r_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}+\dots+r_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}=\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma}\Big(\sum_{i\in J(\gamma)}r_{i}\Big)p_{\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=\bar{\theta}(x)=r_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}+\dots+r_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}=\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma}\Big(\sum_{i\in J(\gamma)}r_{i}\Big)p_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in J(\gamma)}r_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in J(\gamma)}r_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. In view of (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ 2.6.1. Smash products ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.12</span></a>) this implies <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. Thus we have shown that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.
∎</span></p>
