<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a set, we denote by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra obtained from <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> by adjoining the set <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the free product of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and the free <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> generated by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>). If in addition we are given a map <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg:X\to\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg:X\to\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra with the induced grading. We denote by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> the set <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{xp_{\gamma}\mid x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{xp_{\gamma}\mid x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.10</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra where <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a commutative graded ring concentrated in degree <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> a set and <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg:X\to\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg:X\to\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> a map. Consider <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as a <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra with the induced grading. Then</span></p>
