<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 2.8. ‣ 2.6.1. Smash products ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a> that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J</annotation></semantics></math> has the presentation</span></p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J=\Big\langle rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma)\mid{}&amp;rp_{\gamma}+sp_{\gamma}=(r+s)p_{\gamma}\quad(r,s\in R_{\delta};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~rp_{\gamma}sp_{\delta}=rs_{\gamma-\delta}p_{\delta}\quad(r,s\in R^{h};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~(xp_{\gamma})(1p_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}\quad(x\in X,~\gamma\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~(1p_{\gamma+\deg(x)})(xp_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}\quad(x\in X,~\gamma\in\Gamma)\Big\rangle.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>#</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mi>#</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∣</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J=\Big\langle rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma)\mid{}&amp;rp_{\gamma}+sp_{\gamma}=(r+s)p_{\gamma}\quad(r,s\in R_{\delta};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~rp_{\gamma}sp_{\delta}=rs_{\gamma-\delta}p_{\delta}\quad(r,s\in R^{h};~\gamma,\delta\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~(xp_{\gamma})(1p_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}\quad(x\in X,~\gamma\in\Gamma),\\
&amp;~(1p_{\gamma+\deg(x)})(xp_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}\quad(x\in X,~\gamma\in\Gamma)\Big\rangle.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the relations in presentation (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>) above are satisfied in <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J\rightarrow R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J\rightarrow R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">such that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(xp_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(xp_{\gamma})=xp_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly the elements <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> generate the <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(X)\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X)\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. It remains to show that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> be a non-empty and finite word over the alphabet <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{rp_{\gamma},xp_{\gamma}~(r\in R^{h},x\in X,\gamma\in\Gamma)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=y_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}\dots y_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=y_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}\dots y_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1},\dots,y_{n}\in R\cup X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},\dots,y_{n}\in R\cup X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We call <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> a </span><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">path (ending in </span><math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text"> if <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i-1}-\gamma_{i}=\deg(y_{i})~(i=2,\dots,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i-1}-\gamma_{i}=\deg(y_{i})~(i=2,\dots,n)</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the set of of all paths by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, and for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> the set of all paths ending in <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define a map <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta:W\to R\langle X\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta:W\to R\langle X\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(y_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}\dots y_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}})=y_{1}\dots y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(y_{1}p_{\gamma_{1}}\dots y_{n}p_{\gamma_{n}})=y_{1}\dots y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now suppose that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from the presentation (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>) that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\sum_{w\in W}\lambda_{w}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\sum_{w\in W}\lambda_{w}w</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{w}\in k~(w\in W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.330em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{w}\in k~(w\in W)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
