<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w\in W_{\gamma}}\lambda_{w}\zeta(w)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w\in W_{\gamma}}\lambda_{w}\zeta(w)=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks easily that this implies that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w\in W_{\gamma}}\lambda_{w}w=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w\in W_{\gamma}}\lambda_{w}w=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.
∎</span></p>
