<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmthm9" title="Proposition 2.9. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a> that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R\langle X\rangle/I)\#\Gamma\cong R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma/I\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R\langle X\rangle/I)\#\Gamma\cong R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma/I\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Proposition 2.10. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>, there is an isomorphism <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma\to R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma\to R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ideal of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> generated by (<a href="#S2.E14" title="In Corollary 2.11. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.14</span></a>). Hence</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R\langle X\rangle/I)\#\Gamma\cong R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma/I\#\Gamma\cong(R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J^{\prime})/g(I\#\Gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R\langle X\rangle/I)\#\Gamma\cong R\langle X\rangle\#\Gamma/I\#\Gamma\cong(R\#\Gamma\langle X\#\Gamma\rangle/J^{\prime})/g(I\#\Gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The assertion of the corollary follows.
∎</span></p>
