<div id="S3.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a hypergraph and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> an abelian group. For any <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in H^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in H^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> choose an <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{h}\in I_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{h}\in I_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{h}\in J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{h}\in J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. A map <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> which associates to any generator <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}~(h\in H^{1},i\in I_{h},j\in J_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}~(h\in H^{1},i\in I_{h},j\in J_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> an element from <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(h_{ij})=w(h_{ij_{h}})-w(h_{i_{h}j_{h}})+w(h_{i_{h}j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(h_{ij})=w(h_{ij_{h}})-w(h_{i_{h}j_{h}})+w(h_{i_{h}j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in H^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in H^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-weight map</span> for <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Lemma 70]</cite>, a <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-weight map <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> induces a <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-grading on <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(v)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(v)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(h_{ij})=w(h_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(h_{ij})=w(h_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(h_{ij}^{*})=-w(h_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(h_{ij}^{*})=-w(h_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in H^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in H^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in H^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in H^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
