<div id="S3.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Leavitt path algebras)<span id="S3.Thmthm4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">directed graph</span>, i.e. a quadruple <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(E^{0},E^{1},r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(E^{0},E^{1},r,s)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are
sets and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s</annotation></semantics></math> are maps from <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The elements of <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are called <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">vertices</span> and the elements of <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">edges</span>. We may think of an edge <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in E^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in E^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as an arrow from <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(e)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(e)</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">row-finite</em>, i.e. for each vertex <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> there are at most finitely many edges in <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">regular</span> vertices of the graph <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the set of all vertices <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is not the empty set. The <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathsf{k}}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathsf{k}}(E)</annotation></semantics></math> presented by the generating set <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{v,e,e^{*}\mid v\in E^{0},e\in E^{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v,e,e^{*}\mid v\in E^{0},e\in E^{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the relations</p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv=\delta_{uv}u\quad(u,v\in E^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv=\delta_{uv}u\quad(u,v\in E^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s(e)e=e=er(e),~r(e)e^{*}=e^{*}=e^{*}s(e)\quad(e\in E^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(e)e=e=er(e),~r(e)e^{*}=e^{*}=e^{*}s(e)\quad(e\in E^{1})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}ee^{*}=v\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}ee^{*}=v\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{*}f=\delta_{ef}r(e)\quad(e,f\in E^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{*}f=\delta_{ef}r(e)\quad(e,f\in E^{1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is called the <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Leavitt path algebra</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. for example <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>). For each <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> write <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}(v)=\{e^{v,j}\mid j\in J_{v}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}(v)=\{e^{v,j}\mid j\in J_{v}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define a hypergraph <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(H^{0},H^{1},s^{\prime},r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(H^{0},H^{1},s^{\prime},r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}=E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}=E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}=\{h^{v}\mid v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}=\{h^{v}\mid v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(h^{v})=(v)_{i\in\{1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(h^{v})=(v)_{i\in\{1\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}(h^{v})=(r(e^{v,j}))_{j\in J_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(h^{v})=(r(e^{v,j}))_{j\in J_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra isomorphism <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:L_{\mathsf{k}}(E)\rightarrow L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:L_{\mathsf{k}}(E)\rightarrow L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(u)=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(u)=u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(e^{v,j})=h^{v}_{1j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(e^{v,j})=h^{v}_{1j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi((e^{v,j})^{*})=(h^{v}_{1j})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi((e^{v,j})^{*})=(h^{v}_{1j})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Vertex-weighted Leavitt path algebras)<span id="S3.Thmthm5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,w)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">vertex-weighted</span> graph, i.e. <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a directed graph and <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a map associating to each regular vertex a positive integer. We again assume that <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is row-finite. The <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathsf{k}}(E,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathsf{k}}(E,w)</annotation></semantics></math> presented by the generating set <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{v,e_{i},e_{i}^{*}\mid v\in E^{0},e\in E^{1},1\leq i\leq w(s(e))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v,e_{i},e_{i}^{*}\mid v\in E^{0},e\in E^{1},1\leq i\leq w(s(e))\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the relations</p>
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv=\delta_{uv}u\quad(u,v\in E^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv=\delta_{uv}u\quad(u,v\in E^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s(e)e_{i}=e_{i}=e_{i}r(e),~r(e)e_{i}^{*}=e_{i}^{*}=e_{i}^{*}s(e)\quad(e\in E^{1},1\leq i\leq w(s(e)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(e)e_{i}=e_{i}=e_{i}r(e),~r(e)e_{i}^{*}=e_{i}^{*}=e_{i}^{*}s(e)\quad(e\in E^{1},1\leq i\leq w(s(e)))</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}e_{i}e_{j}^{*}=\delta_{ij}v\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}};~1\leq i,j\leq w(v))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}e_{i}e_{j}^{*}=\delta_{ij}v\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}};~1\leq i,j\leq w(v))</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{1\leq i\leq w(v)}e_{i}^{*}f_{i}=\delta_{ef}r(e)\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}};~e,f\in s^{-1}(v))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{1\leq i\leq w(v)}e_{i}^{*}f_{i}=\delta_{ef}r(e)\quad(v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}};~e,f\in s^{-1}(v))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is called the <span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Leavitt path algebra</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,w)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> write <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}(v)=\{e^{v,j}\mid j\in J_{v}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}(v)=\{e^{v,j}\mid j\in J_{v}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define a hypergraph <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(H^{0},H^{1},s^{\prime},r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(H^{0},H^{1},s^{\prime},r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}=E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}=E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}=\{h^{v}\mid v\in E^{0}_{\operatorname{reg}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}=\{h^{v}\mid v\in E^{0}_{\operatorname{reg}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(h^{v})=(v)_{i\in\{1,\dots,w(v)\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(h^{v})=(v)_{i\in\{1,\dots,w(v)\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}(h^{v})=(r(e^{v,j}))_{j\in J_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(h^{v})=(r(e^{v,j}))_{j\in J_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra isomorphism <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:L_{\mathsf{k}}(E,w)\rightarrow L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:L_{\mathsf{k}}(E,w)\rightarrow L_{\mathsf{k}}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(u)=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(u)=u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(e^{v,j}_{i})=h^{v}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(e^{v,j}_{i})=h^{v}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi((e^{v,j}_{i})^{*})=(h^{v}_{ij})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi((e^{v,j}_{i})^{*})=(h^{v}_{ij})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,w(v)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,w(v)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
