<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Bergman algebras</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a ring and <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathbb{M}_{m}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathbb{M}_{m}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> be idempotent matrices. Recall that <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> are called <em id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">equivalent</em>, denoted <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\sim f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\sim f</annotation></semantics></math>, if there are matrices <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathbb{M}_{m\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}\in M_{n\times m}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}\in M_{n\times m}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=hh^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=hh^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=h^{*}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=h^{*}h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_deff">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra, where <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a commutative ring. Let <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathbb{M}_{m}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathbb{M}_{m}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{M}_{n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> be idempotent matrices. Let <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(h_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(h_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}=(h^{*}_{ji})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}=(h^{*}_{ji})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, be a collection of symbols. Then we define a chain of <em id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Bergman algebras</em></p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{1}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B^{2}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B^{3}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B_{R}(e,f)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{1}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B^{2}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B^{3}_{R}(e,f)\longrightarrow B_{R}(e,f),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
