<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and a graded idempotent endomorphism <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e:F\xrightarrow{}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e:F\xrightarrow{}F</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\circ e=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\circ e=e</annotation></semantics></math>). Set <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:={\rm Im}\,e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:={\rm Im}\,e</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:M\xrightarrow{}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:M\xrightarrow{}P</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:X\xrightarrow{}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:X\xrightarrow{}F</annotation></semantics></math> in the following diagram</span></p>
