<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfying <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ u=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ u=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-e)\circ h=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-e)\circ h=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\circ h=g\circ\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\circ h=g\circ\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, for any graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:X\xrightarrow{}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:X\xrightarrow{}F</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ u=0=(1-e)\circ h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ u=0=(1-e)\circ h</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:M\xrightarrow{}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:M\xrightarrow{}P</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\circ h=g\circ\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\circ h=g\circ\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we have that <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:M\xrightarrow{}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:M\xrightarrow{}P</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero map if and only if the corresponding <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:X\xrightarrow{}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:X\xrightarrow{}F</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero map.</span></p>
</div>
