<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle u}}{{\longrightarrow}}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\varepsilon}}{{\longrightarrow}}M\longrightarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>u</mi></mover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>ε</mi></mover><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{i\in I}R(\alpha_{i})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle u}}{{\longrightarrow}}\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\varepsilon}}{{\longrightarrow}}M\longrightarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">is an exact sequence of graded <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. Using the matrix representation of §<a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, we have</span></p>
