<p id="S5.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}=(\alpha_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{j})_{j\in J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\beta}=(\beta_{j})_{j\in J}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also write <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> as a direct summand of a graded free <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> (see (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>)). Hence, <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as the image of a graded idempotent endomorphism <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e:\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e:\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{m\in K}R(\gamma_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, by §<a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> we have <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e=(v_{mm^{\prime}})_{m,m^{\prime}\in K}\in\mathbb{M}_{K\times K}(R)[\overline{\gamma}][\overline{\gamma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e=(v_{mm^{\prime}})_{m,m^{\prime}\in K}\in\mathbb{M}_{K\times K}(R)[\overline{\gamma}][\overline{\gamma}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\gamma}=(\gamma_{m})_{m\in K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\gamma}=(\gamma_{m})_{m\in K}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and any graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:T\otimes_{R}M\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:T\otimes_{R}M\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R}P</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following diagram with the first two rows exact</span></p>
