<p id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The desired <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> has the graded <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-homomorphism <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\xrightarrow{}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\xrightarrow{}S</annotation></semantics></math> which sends <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" disp