<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra, <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> a graded <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module, <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> a graded projective <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module, and <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:M\xrightarrow{}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:M\xrightarrow{}P</annotation></semantics></math> a graded module homomorphism. Then there exists a <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\otimes_{R}f=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\otimes_{R}f=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is universal for this property: Given any <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\otimes_{R}f=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\otimes_{R}f=0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a unique graded homomorphism of <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-rings}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-rings</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-rings}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\xrightarrow{}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\xrightarrow{}T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
