<p id="S5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where by Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely determined by a graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ\overline{u_{0}}=0=\overline{1-e_{0}}\circ h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ\overline{u_{0}}=0=\overline{1-e_{0}}\circ h</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
