<p id="S5.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra. One observes that by the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> the elements of the matrix <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> as additional generators of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> are of zero degree. By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, it follows that the universal homomorphism of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of the universal homomorphism of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> to the zeroth component.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we prove that
<math id="S5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\ast_{R_{0}}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\cong R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\ast_{R_{0}}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\cong R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras. One notes that we have the natural inclusion <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota:R_{0}\xrightarrow{}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota:R_{0}\xrightarrow{}R</annotation></semantics></math>, and the natural homomorphisms <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi:R_{0}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:R_{0}\xrightarrow{}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> sending <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\prime}:R\xrightarrow{}R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}:R\xrightarrow{}R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> sending <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The homomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varphi:R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\xrightarrow{}R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\xrightarrow{}R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is induced by the homomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\langle h_{0}\rangle\xrightarrow{}R\langle h\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\langle h_{0}\rangle\xrightarrow{}R\langle h\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> since the matrix <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is induced by <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, equivalently, we have <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{0})=r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{0})=r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}\in R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}\in R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(h_{ij})=h_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(h_{ij})=h_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}=(h_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}=(h_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows directly that in the diagram below, <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\circ\pi=\pi^{\prime}\circ\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\circ\pi=\pi^{\prime}\circ\iota</annotation></semantics></math>. In order to prove that <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the coproduct <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R*_{R_{0}}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R*_{R_{0}}R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, one only needs to check that <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle f:\overline{M}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> has the universal property. That is, taking any <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and any homomorphisms <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m26" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha:R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\xrightarrow{}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:R_{0}\langle f_{0}:\overline{M_{0}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{0}}\rangle\xrightarrow{}S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:R\xrightarrow{}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:R\xrightarrow{}S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" altte