<div id="S5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a strongly <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded finitely generated projective <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finitely generated projective <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-module. We write <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as the summand of the free <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fact that it is a direct summand insures that for any
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ring</mi><msub><mi>𝗄</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{i}:T\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{i}:T\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the inclusion <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:P_{0}\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:P_{0}\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is again an inclusion. Hence if we write for each <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\in M_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\in M_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}(m_{0})=\sum_{c\in C}f_{m_{0},c}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}(m_{0})=\sum_{c\in C}f_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> in the component <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. We can see that for any <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ring</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> will be zero if and only
if all the <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> go to zero in <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\langle\overline{f_{0}}=0\rangle\cong R_{0}/\langle f_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\langle\overline{f_{0}}=0\rangle\cong R_{0}/\langle f_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the two-sided ideal of <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the elements <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">One observes that <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a direct summand of the free <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})\cong\bigoplus_{c\in C}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})\cong\bigoplus_{c\in C}R</annotation></semantics></math>. Actually we have the maps</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\otimes_{R_{0}}M_{0}\longrightarrow{}R\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}\longrightarrow{}R\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})\cong\bigoplus_{c\in C}R." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\otimes_{R_{0}}M_{0}\longrightarrow{}R\otimes_{R_{0}}P_{0}\longrightarrow{}R\otimes_{R_{0}}(\bigoplus_{c\in C}R_{0})\cong\bigoplus_{c\in C}R.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">We write for each <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\in M_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\in M_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0}(r\otimes m_{0})=\sum_{c\in C}rf_{m_{0},c}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0}(r\otimes m_{0})=\sum_{c\in C}rf_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R</annotation></semantics></math> a homogeneous element, and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> in the component <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ring</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}{\rm ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}\otimes_{R}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}\otimes_{R}f</annotation></semantics></math> will be zero if and only
if <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}\otimes_{R}(R\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}\otimes_{R}(R\otimes_{R_{0}}f_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> will be zero, if and only if all the <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rf_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rf_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> go to zero in <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for any homogeneous elements <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\in M_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\in M_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle\overline{f}=0\rangle\cong R/\langle rf_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{r\in R_{h},m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle\overline{f}=0\rangle\cong R/\langle rf_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{r\in R_{h},m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set consisting of all homogeneous elements of <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle rf_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle rf_{m_{0},c}\rangle_{m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the two-sided ideal of <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the homogeneous elements <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rf_{m_{0},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rf_{m_{0},c}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\in M_{0},c\in C</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we have</span></p>
