<p id="S5.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">One observes that we obtain the following commutative diagram with <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}(r)=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}(r)=r</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1}(\overline{r_{0}})=\overline{r_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1}(\overline{r_{0}})=\overline{r_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}\in R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}\in R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
