<p id="S5.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">as the projective resolution of <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> as graded <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. Writing <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\bigoplus Q^{\prime}\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}\bigoplus_{i=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⨁</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>gr</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\bigoplus Q^{\prime}\cong_{\operatorname{gr}}\bigoplus_{i=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>,
by the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, for any <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and any graded module homomorphsm <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}:T\otimes_{R}P\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>P</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}:T\otimes_{R}P\xrightarrow{}T\otimes_{R}Q</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following diagram with the first two rows exact</span></p>
