<div id="S5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (1), by matrix relations (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>), we have the multiplication of matrices
<math id="S5.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-e)h=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-e)h=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(1-f)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(1-f)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to that <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ehf=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ehf=h</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle i:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle i:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle h\rangle/{\langle ehf=h\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle h\rangle/{\langle ehf=h\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (2), by Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, for <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:P\rightarrow Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:P\rightarrow Q</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{k=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{k=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{g}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 5.4. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> the desired universal ring <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle\overline{g}=0\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle\overline{g}=0\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the quotient of <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> by the two-sided ideal generated by entries of the matrix <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We have the following two consequences which will be used in the following subsections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.8</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra and let <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be non-zero graded finitely generated projective <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules.
We have the <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded algebra isomorphism</span></p>
