<div id="S5.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 5.7. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>(1) we have that <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle i_{0}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q},i_{0}^{\prime}:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle\cong R\langle h,h^{*}\rangle/\langle ehf=h,fh^{*}e=h^{*}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle i_{0}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q},i_{0}^{\prime}:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle\cong R\langle h,h^{*}\rangle/\langle ehf=h,fh^{*}e=h^{*}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Now for the <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-gr-rings}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-gr-rings</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-gr-rings}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S=R\langle i_{0}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q},i_{0}^{\prime}:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=R\langle i_{0}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{Q},i_{0}^{\prime}:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following two diagrams (see (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>))</span></p>
