alttext="\operatorname{id}_{S\otimes P}-i_{0}^{\prime}\circ i_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{id}_{S\otimes P}-i_{0}^{\prime}\circ i_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding matrix representation of <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e-h^{*}\circ h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e-h^{*}\circ h</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e-hh^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e-hh^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (see <a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.3. Matrix form of graded homomorphisms ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>). Similarly one can show that <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-h^{*}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-h^{*}h</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding matrix of <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{id}_{S\otimes Q}-i_{0}\circ i_{0}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{id}_{S\otimes Q}-i_{0}\circ i_{0}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 5.7. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>(2), we then have</span></p>
