<div id="S5.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra and <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> a non-zero graded finitely generated projective <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. We have the <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded algebra isomorphism</span></p>
