<p id="S5.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 5.7. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>(1) we have that <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\langle i^{\prime}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle\cong R\langle h\rangle/\langle ehe=h\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle i^{\prime}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle\cong R\langle h\rangle/\langle ehe=h\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Now for the graded <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S^{\prime}=R\langle i^{\prime}:\overline{P}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo>