<p id="S5.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">with the first two rows exact, the right square commutative and <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-e)h=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-e)h=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(1-e)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(1-e)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-h^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-h^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the matrix of <math id="S5.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}-i^{\prime}\circ i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}-i^{\prime}\circ i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>). Now by Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 5.7. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>(2), the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
