<div id="S5.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Given a graded homomorphism <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:P\xrightarrow{}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:P\xrightarrow{}Q</annotation></semantics></math> between graded finitely generated projective <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, we may construct a <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>-ring</mtext><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle\overline{g}^{-1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle\overline{g}^{-1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> in which <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{g}</annotation></semantics></math> become an isomorphism, by adjoining a map <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\overline{Q}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, then setting <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{\overline{P}}-g\circ\overline{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{\overline{P}}-g\circ\overline{g}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{\overline{Q}}-\overline{g}\circ g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{\overline{Q}}-\overline{g}\circ g</annotation></semantics></math> equal to zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that by Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> there is a unique graded homomorphism <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}:\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\beta_{j})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{k=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}:\bigoplus_{j=1}^{n}R(\beta_{j})\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{k=1}^{m}R(\gamma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:P\xrightarrow{}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:P\xrightarrow{}Q</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="eh_{g}f=h_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">eh_{g}f=h_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can describe the universal localisation algebra of the <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module homomorphism <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:P\rightarrow Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:P\rightarrow Q</annotation></semantics></math> as follows (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, page 293]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.10</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra and <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:P\xrightarrow{}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:P\xrightarrow{}Q</annotation></semantics></math> a graded <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module homomorphism.
We have the <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded algebra isomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\big\langle\overline{g}^{-1}\big\rangle\cong R\big\langle h^{*}\big\rangle/\big\langle fh^{*}e=h,h_{g}h^{*}=e,h^{*}h_{g}=f\big\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\big\langle\overline{g}^{-1}\big\rangle\cong R\big\langle h^{*}\big\rangle/\big\langle fh^{*}e=h,h_{g}h^{*}=e,h^{*}h_{g}=f\big\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
