<p id="S5.SS4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="S5.SS4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded <math id="S5.SS4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>ring</mtext></mrow><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the graded algebra homomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}:R\xrightarrow{}S_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}:R\xrightarrow{}S_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS4.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> be the graded <math id="S5.SS4.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Sigma}\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>ring</mtext></mrow><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Sigma}\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
