<div id="S5.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we prove that <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> has the universal property of <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any graded <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Sigma}\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>ring</mtext></mrow><mi>𝗄</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Sigma}\text{-}\text{ring}_{\mathsf{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\otimes(1-\Delta_{\xi}\circ(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\otimes(1-\Delta_{\xi}\circ(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi))=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\otimes(1-(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi)\circ\Delta_{\xi})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\otimes(1-(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi)\circ\Delta_{\xi})=0,</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a unique graded algebra homomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:S\xrightarrow{}{}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:S\xrightarrow{}{}T</annotation></semantics></math> in the following diagram</span></p>
