<div id="S5.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We are in a position to extend <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Proposition 3.1 (1)]</cite>, which only worked for <math id="S5.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded algebras. The existence of a <math id="S5.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded universal localization follows from the argument in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite> adapted for categories with automorphisms. Here we prove that the existence of any <math id="S5.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded universal localization follows from graded Bergman’s constructions where <math id="S5.SS4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is any abelian group.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that a <math id="S5.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded ring <math id="S5.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> (with unit) is called left graded hereditary if any graded submodule of a graded projective left <math id="S5.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module is (graded) projective, which is equivalent to that the graded global dimension for <math id="S5.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> being less than or equal to <math id="S5.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (see §<a href="#S2.SS5" title="2.5. Graded hereditary rings ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.13</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be an abelian group, <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> a <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra and <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> a family of morphisms between <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded finitely generated projective <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. We have the following statements.</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The induced homomorphism </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\xrightarrow{}R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\xrightarrow{}R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\mapsto\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\mapsto\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, is a </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-graded universal localization of </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with respect to </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and is unique up to isomorphism.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the underlying homomorphism </span><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\Sigma}:R\xrightarrow{}R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\Sigma}:R\xrightarrow{}R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of ungraded algebras is a universal localization of </span><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with respect to </span><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=U(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=U(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which is the image of </span><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under the forgetful functor </span><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is graded hereditary, so is </span><math id="S5.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\langle{\overline{\xi}}^{-1}\rangle_{\xi\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) Recall from (<a href="#S5.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.4. Universal morphisms and representable functors ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a>) that <math id="S5.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{\Sigma}=R\langle\Delta_{\xi}:\overline{Q_{\xi}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{\xi}}|\xi:P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}Q_{\xi}\in\Sigma\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Sigma}=R\langle\Delta_{\xi}:\overline{Q_{\xi}}\xrightarrow{}\overline{P_{\xi}}|\xi:P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}Q_{\xi}\in\Sigma\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="S5.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}\xi:R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{\sim}R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}Q_{\xi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}\xi:R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{\sim}R_{\Sigma}\otimes_{R}Q_{\xi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">is an isomorphism for each <math id="S5.SS4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi:P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}Q_{\xi}\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi:P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}Q_{\xi}\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-inverting graded homomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}:R\xrightarrow{}S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}:R\xrightarrow{}S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a unique graded <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:S_{\Sigma}\xrightarrow{}{}S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:S_{\Sigma}\xrightarrow{}{}S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)^{-1}=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)^{-1}=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}=\lambda\circ\theta_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}=\lambda\circ\theta_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the isomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi:S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}{}S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}Q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi:S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}P_{\xi}\xrightarrow{}{}S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}Q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}1-(S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi})\circ(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}(1-\Delta_{\xi}\circ(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi))=0;\\
1-(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)\circ(S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi})=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}(1-(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi)\circ\Delta_{\xi})=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}1-(S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi})\circ(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}(1-\Delta_{\xi}\circ(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi))=0;\\
1-(S^{\prime}\otimes_{R}\xi)\circ(S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}\Delta_{\xi})=S^{\prime}\otimes_{\lambda}(1-(S_{\Sigma}\otimes_{\theta_{1}}\xi)\circ\Delta_{\xi})=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">There exists a unique graded <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S5.SS4.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:R_{\Sigma}\xrightarrow{}S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:R_{\Sigma}\xrightarrow{}S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following diagram.</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

