<p id="S5.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}(R/p_{r(e)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}(R/p_{r(e)})</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}\bigoplus Q=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}\bigoplus Q=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">that is, the second row of the above diagram splits. And <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is an idempotent endomorphism of <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R(1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{v}|_{Q(1)}=\operatorname{id}_{Q(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{v}|_{Q(1)}=\operatorname{id}_{Q(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Ker}f^{v}=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Ker}f^{v}=\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the graded module homomorphism <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as the matrix</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}{e_{1}^{v}}\\
e_{2}^{v}\\
\vdots\\
e_{n_{v}}^{v}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}{e_{1}^{v}}\\
e_{2}^{v}\\
\vdots\\
e_{n_{v}}^{v}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">such that <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}^{v},e_{2}^{v},\cdots,e_{n_{v}}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}^{v},e_{2}^{v},\cdots,e_{n_{v}}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> are elements in <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the index set of all the edges starting from <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1. Graded universal morphisms ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, the universal algebra <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with universal graded module homomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{v}:S\otimes_{R}p_{v}\longrightarrow S\otimes_{R}\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⊗</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>R</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{v}:S\otimes_{R}p_{v}\longrightarrow S\otimes_{R}\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">for regular vertices <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained via adjoining to <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> generators <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>reg</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{\operatorname{reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the relations <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{v}\circ u=0=f^{v}\circ h^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{v}\circ u=0=f^{v}\circ h^{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, we have <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{v}\circ u=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{v}\circ u=0</annotation></semantics></math> implying</span></p>
<table id="S5.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{e}}_{w}e^{v}_{i}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{e}}_{w}e^{v}_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\neq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\neq v</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0,\cdots,0,1,0\cdots,0\end{pmatrix}\in p_{w}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0,\cdots,0,1,0\cdots,0\end{pmatrix}\in p_{w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Hence by the universal property of the cokernel <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a unique graded homomorphism <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:p_{v}\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:p_{v}\xrightarrow{}\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}R(1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{v}=\tau\circ\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{v}=\tau\circ\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. This deduce that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{v}e_{i}^{v}=e^{v}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{v}e_{i}^{v}=e^{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also we have <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{v}\circ h^{v}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{v}\circ h^{v}=0</annotation></semantics></math> implying</span></p>
<table id="S5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{v}_{i}\mathbf{e}_{r(e^{v}_{i})}=e^{v}_{i},\qquad e^{v}_{i}{\mathbf{e}}_{w}=0\text{~for~}w\neq r(e^{v}_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{v}_{i}\mathbf{e}_{r(e^{v}_{i})}=e^{v}_{i},\qquad e^{v}_{i}{\mathbf{e}}_{w}=0\text{~for~}w\neq r(e^{v}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
