<div id="S5.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We have the following consequence (compare with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Proposition 4.3(1)]</cite>). We mention that in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> the authors constructed the maps <math id="S5.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> which are exactly the graded universal homomorphisms of Bergman algebras.</p>
</div>
