<p id="S6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> as the image of an idempotent graded endomorphism <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> of a graded free <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module of finite rank <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> as the image of an idempotent graded endomorphism <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> of a graded free <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module of finite rank <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{m\in M}R(\gamma_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{m\in M}R(\gamma_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(d_{ij})=\beta_{j}-\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(d_{ij})=\beta_{j}-\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in J</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(e_{km})=\gamma_{m}-\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(e_{km})=\gamma_{m}-\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,m\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,m\in M</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 5.8. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a> that <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained from <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> by adjoining homogeneous generators <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{jm},h^{\prime}_{mj}~(j\in J,m\in M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{jm},h^{\prime}_{mj}~(j\in J,m\in M)</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(h_{jm})=\gamma_{m}-\beta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(h_{jm})=\gamma_{m}-\beta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(h^{\prime}_{mj})=\beta_{j}-\gamma_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(h^{\prime}_{mj})=\beta_{j}-\gamma_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and relations <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dh=h=he,~eh^{\prime}=h^{\prime}=h^{\prime}d,~hh^{\prime}=d,~h^{\prime}h=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dh=h=he,~eh^{\prime}=h^{\prime}=h^{\prime}d,~hh^{\prime}=d,~h^{\prime}h=e</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cong R\langle X\rangle/I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cong R\langle X\rangle/I</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS1