<p id="S6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It follows from Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 2.8. ‣ 2.6.1. Smash products ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S2.Thmthm11" title="Corollary 2.11. ‣ 2.6.2. Smash products of quotients and extensions ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.11</span></a> that <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has the presentation</p>
