<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma_{A}=\{\gamma-\gamma_{m},\gamma-\beta_{j}\mid\gamma\in A,j\in J,m\in M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{A}=\{\gamma-\gamma_{m},\gamma-\beta_{j}\mid\gamma\in A,j\in J,m\in M\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a unital algebra with identity <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo>→</mo></munder><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> runs through all finite subsets of <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show that the <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are isomorphic to Bergman algebras.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> a finite subset. We denote by <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> the subalgebra of <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of all sums of elements <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rp_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rp_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is is a unital algebra with identity <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> has the presentation</span></p>
<table id="S6.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}R\#\Gamma_{A}=\Big\langle&amp;rp_{\beta}\quad(r\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A})\mid{}\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}+sp_{\beta}=(r+s)p_{\beta}\quad(r,s\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}),\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}sp_{\beta^{\prime}}=rs_{\beta-\beta^{\prime}}p_{\beta^{\prime}}\quad(r\in R_{\alpha};~s\in R_{\alpha^{\prime}};~\alpha+\beta,\beta,\alpha^{\prime}+\beta^{\prime},\beta^{\prime}\in\Gamma_{A})\Big\rangle.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>#</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∣</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}R\#\Gamma_{A}=\Big\langle&amp;rp_{\beta}\quad(r\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A})\mid{}\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}+sp_{\beta}=(r+s)p_{\beta}\quad(r,s\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}),\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}sp_{\beta^{\prime}}=rs_{\beta-\beta^{\prime}}p_{\beta^{\prime}}\quad(r\in R_{\alpha};~s\in R_{\alpha^{\prime}};~\alpha+\beta,\beta,\alpha^{\prime}+\beta^{\prime},\beta^{\prime}\in\Gamma_{A})\Big\rangle.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra presented by (<a href="#S6.E4" title="In Lemma 6.1. ‣ 6.1. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras I ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>). It follows from Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 2.8. ‣ 2.6.1. Smash products ‣ 2.6. Smash products of graded algebras ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a> that there is a <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:Z\to R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:Z\to R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(rp_{\gamma})=rp_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly one can write any element <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in Z</annotation></semantics></math> in the form <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\sum_{\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}\sum_{\alpha+\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}r_{\beta}^{(\alpha)}p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\sum_{\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}\sum_{\alpha+\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}r_{\beta}^{(\alpha)}p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}\in R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}\in R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(Z)=R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(Z)=R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to show that <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. Suppose that <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in Z</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\sum_{\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}\sum_{\alpha+\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}r_{\beta}^{(\alpha)}p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\sum_{\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}\sum_{\alpha+\beta\in\Gamma_{A}}r_{\beta}^{(\alpha)}p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}\in R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}\in R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that each <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(\alpha)}_{\beta}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is injective and therefore <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\cong\phi(Z)=R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\cong\phi(Z)=R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A</annotation></semantics></math> define the matrices</p>
<table id="S6.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=(d_{ij}^{(\gamma)})_{i,j\in J}=(d_{ij}p_{\gamma-\beta_{j}})_{i,j\in J}\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{J\times J}(R\#\Gamma_{A})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=(d_{ij}^{(\gamma)})_{i,j\in J}=(d_{ij}p_{\gamma-\beta_{j}})_{i,j\in J}\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{J\times J}(R\#\Gamma_{A}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=(e_{km}^{(\gamma)})_{k,m\in K}=(e_{km}p_{\gamma-\gamma_{m}})_{k,m\in K}\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{M\times M}(R\#\Gamma_{A})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=(e_{km}^{(\gamma)})_{k,m\in K}=(e_{km}p_{\gamma-\gamma_{m}})_{k,m\in K}\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{M\times M}(R\#\Gamma_{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">A straightforward computation shows that <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> are idempotent matrices. Hence they define idempotent endomorphisms of <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. It follows that <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma_{A})d^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma_{A})d^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A}^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma_{A})e^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A}^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma_{A})e^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-zero finitely generated projective <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. Define the <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra</p>
<table id="S6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{A}:=R\#\Gamma_{A}\Big\langle g^{(\gamma)},(g^{(\gamma)})^{-1}:\overline{P_{A}^{(\gamma)}}\cong\overline{Q_{A}^{(\gamma)}}~(\gamma\in A)\Big\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>#</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>≅</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{A}:=R\#\Gamma_{A}\Big\langle g^{(\gamma)},(g^{(\gamma)})^{-1}:\overline{P_{A}^{(\gamma)}}\cong\overline{Q_{A}^{(\gamma)}}~(\gamma\in A)\Big\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">We will show that <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}\cong B_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}\cong B_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 5.8. ‣ 5.3. Matrix forms for three types of Bergman algebras ‣ 5. Graded Bergman universal construction ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a> and (<a href="#S6.E4" title="In Lemma 6.1. ‣ 6.1. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras I ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>) we have</p>
<table id="S6.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}B_{A}=\Big\langle&amp;rp_{\beta}~(r\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A});~~~~g^{(\gamma)}_{jm},(g^{\prime})^{(\gamma)}_{mj}~~(\gamma\in A,j\in J,m\in M)\mid{}\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}+sp_{\beta}=(r+s)p_{\beta}\quad(r,s\in R_{\alpha};~\alpha+\beta,\beta\in\Gamma_{A}),\\
&amp;rp_{\beta}sp_{\beta^{\prime}}=rs_{\beta-\beta^{\prime}}p_{\beta^{\prime}}\quad(r\in R_{\alpha};~s\in R_{\alpha^{\prime}};~\alpha+\beta,\beta,\alpha^{\prime}+\beta^{\prime},\beta^{\prime}\in\Gamma_{A}),\\
&amp;\sum_{i\in J}d^{(\gamma)}_{ji}g_{im}^{(\gamma)}=g_{jm}^{(\gamma)}=\sum_{k\in M}g_{jk}^{(\gamma)}e_{km}^{(\gamma)}\quad(j\in J,m\in M,\gamma\in A),\\
&amp;\sum_{k\in M}e_{mk}^{(\gamma)}(g^{\prime}_{kj})^{(\gamma)}=(g^{\prime}_{mj})^{(\gamma)}=\sum_{i\in J}(g^{\prime})_{mi}^{(\gamma)}d_{ij}^{(\gamma)}\quad(j\in J,m\in M,\gamma\in A),\\
&amp;\sum_{m\in M}g_{im}^{(\gamma)}(g^{\prime})^{(\gamma)}_{mj}=d_{ij}^{(\gamma)}\quad(i,j\in J;~\gamma\in A),\\
