<div id="S6.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We finish this subsection by proving a lemma which will be used in §7. For <math id="S6.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> we define the <math id="S6.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S6.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma)d^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma)d^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma)e^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(\gamma)}:=(\bigoplus_{m\in M}R\#\Gamma)e^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(\gamma)}\cong P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(\gamma)}\cong P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(\gamma)}\cong Q(-\gamma)\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(\gamma)}\cong Q(-\gamma)\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-modules.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only prove that <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma\cong P^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma\cong P^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof that <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(-\gamma)\#\Gamma\cong Q^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(-\gamma)\#\Gamma\cong Q^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> is similar. Recall that</span></p>
