<p id="S6.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">as a set. Hence any element of <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(-\gamma)\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xd</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the map</span></p>
