<p id="S6.SS1.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R(\beta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.SS1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined and injective.</span></p>
