<div id="S6.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we show that <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. Let <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in P^{(\gamma)}=\operatorname{Im}(d^{(\gamma)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in P^{(\gamma)}=\operatorname{Im}(d^{(\gamma)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\bigoplus_{j\in J}R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=yd^{(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=yd^{(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in J</annotation></semantics></math> write <math id="S6.SS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=\sum_{\alpha\in\Gamma}y_{i,\alpha}p_{\alpha}\in R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=\sum_{\alpha\in\Gamma}y_{i,\alpha}p_{\alpha}\in R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
