<p id="S6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma_{A}=\{\gamma-\beta_{j}\mid\gamma\in A,j\in J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{A}=\{\gamma-\beta_{j}\mid\gamma\in A,j\in J\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a unital algebra with identity <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{A}}p_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo>→</mo></munder><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> runs through all finite subsets of <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show that the <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are isomorphic to Bergman algebras.</p>
