<div id="S6.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6.8</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite subset. Then <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{A}\cong B_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{A}\cong B_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proposition follows from (<a href="#S6.E18" title="In 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.18</span></a>), (<a href="#S6.E20" title="In 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.20</span></a>) and (<a href="#S6.E21" title="In Lemma 6.7. ‣ 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.21</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The theorem below is the main result of this subsection. It follows directly from Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm8" title="Proposition 6.8. ‣ 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a> and the fact that <math id="S6.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo>→</mo></munder><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\#\Gamma=\varinjlim_{A}T_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> runs through all finite subsets of <math id="S6.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.9</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\big\langle e:\overline{P}\to\overline{P};~e^{2}=e\big\rangle\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.497em">;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\big\langle e:\overline{P}\to\overline{P};~e^{2}=e\big\rangle\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct limit of the Bergman algebras</span></p>
