<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7. </span>The graded <math id="S7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra</h2>

<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1. </span>Basic definitions and results</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a not necessarily unital ring. Recall that a <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unital</span> if <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RM=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RM=M</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}</annotation></semantics></math> the category of unital <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. Furthermore, we denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math> the full subcategory of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose objects are the projective objects of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}</annotation></semantics></math> that are finitely generated as a <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. If <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> has local units, we define</p>
<table id="S7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(R)=\{[P]\mid P\in R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(R)=\{[P]\mid P\in R\text{-}\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the isomorphism class of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> as a <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> becomes an abelian monoid by defining <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P]+[Q]=[P\oplus Q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P]+[Q]=[P\oplus Q]</annotation></semantics></math>. It is well-known that <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is a functor that commutes with direct limits. There is a different, but equivalent definition of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> using idempotent matrices over <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Subsection 4A]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> now be a <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded ring. Recall that a <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is called <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-graded</span> if there is a decomposition <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\bigoplus_{\gamma\in\Gamma}M_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\bigoplus_{\gamma\in\Gamma}M_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}M_{\gamma}\subseteq M_{\alpha\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}M_{\gamma}\subseteq M_{\alpha\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}</annotation></semantics></math> the category of <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded unital <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules with morphisms the <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module homomorphisms that preserve grading. Moreover, we denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math> the full subcategory of <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose objects are the projective objects of <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}</annotation></semantics></math> that are finitely generated as a <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. If <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> has graded local units, we define</p>
