<div id="S7.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Proposition 66]</cite>)<span id="S7.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded ring with graded local units. Then <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\cong R\#\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆𝐫</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Gr}}_{\operatorname{proj}}\cong R\#\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mi>proj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{{\bf Mod}}_{\operatorname{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math> by an isomorphism that commutes with direct sums. It follows that <math id="S7.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\cong\mathcal{V}(R\#\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\cong\mathcal{V}(R\#\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a unital ring and <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> an idempotent matrix. Then <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> defines an endomorphism of the <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we also denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly the image <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is a finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module (since <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{n}=\operatorname{Ker}\epsilon\oplus\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{n}=\operatorname{Ker}\epsilon\oplus\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>). Now let <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. Then <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\oplus N=R^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\oplus N=R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define an endomorphism <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon|_{M}=\operatorname{id}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon|_{M}=\operatorname{id}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon|_{N}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon|_{N}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then clearly <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is idempotent. We denote the idempotent matrix in <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> also by <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)=M</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence any finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module equals <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for some idempotent square matrix <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now let <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded ring and <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> an idempotent matrix with homogeneous entries such <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> defines an endomorphism of the graded <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we also denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly the image <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module (since <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})=\operatorname{Ker}\epsilon\oplus\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})=\operatorname{Ker}\epsilon\oplus\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>). Now let <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a graded finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module. Then <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\oplus N=\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\oplus N=\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> for some graded <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Define an endomorphism <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{k=1}^{n}R(\gamma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon|_{M}=\operatorname{id}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon|_{M}=\operatorname{id}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon|_{N}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon|_{N}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then clearly <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\operatorname{Im}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is idempotent. We denote the idempotent matrix in <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> also by <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)=M</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence any graded finitely generated projective <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module equals <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for some idempotent square matrix <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS1.p4.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded ring and <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> an idempotent matrix with homogeneous entries such <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\epsilon)\#\Gamma\cong M(\epsilon\#\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\epsilon)\#\Gamma\cong M(\epsilon\#\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\#\Gamma\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\#\Gamma\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="S7.Thmthm2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon\#\Gamma)_{ij}=\epsilon_{ij}p_{-\gamma_{j}}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon\#\Gamma)_{ij}=\epsilon_{ij}p_{-\gamma_{j}}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
