<div id="S7.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.3</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:R\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:R\to S</annotation></semantics></math> be a ring homomorphism and <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> an idempotent matrix. Then <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\cong M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\cong M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\epsilon)\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\epsilon)\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by applying <math id="S7.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to each entry.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that as an abelian monoid, <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> has the presentation</span></p>
<table id="S7.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Big\langle s\otimes m~(s\in S,m\in M(\epsilon))\mid{}&amp;(s_{1}+s_{2})\otimes m=s_{1}\otimes m+s_{2}\otimes m~(s_{1},s_{2}\in S;~m\in M(\epsilon)),\\
&amp;s\otimes(m_{1}+m_{2})=s\otimes m_{1}+s\otimes m_{2}~(s\in S;~m_{1},m_{2}\in M(\epsilon)),\\
&amp;s.r\otimes m=s\otimes r.m~(s\in S;~r\in R;~m\in M(\epsilon))\Big\rangle.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.660em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∣</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.660em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.660em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Big\langle s\otimes m~(s\in S,m\in M(\epsilon))\mid{}&amp;(s_{1}+s_{2})\otimes m=s_{1}\otimes m+s_{2}\otimes m~(s_{1},s_{2}\in S;~m\in M(\epsilon)),\\
&amp;s\otimes(m_{1}+m_{2})=s\otimes m_{1}+s\otimes m_{2}~(s\in S;~m_{1},m_{2}\in M(\epsilon)),\\
&amp;s.r\otimes m=s\otimes r.m~(s\in S;~r\in R;~m\in M(\epsilon))\Big\rangle.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly for any <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,l\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,l\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> induces a map <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{k\times l}(R)\to\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{k\times l}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{k\times l}(R)\to\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{k\times l}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, which we also denote by <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. We define a monoid homomorphism <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> from the free abelian monoid <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\langle s\otimes m~(s\in S,m\in M(\epsilon))\big\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.330em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\langle s\otimes m~(s\in S,m\in M(\epsilon))\big\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> to the abelian monoid <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(s\otimes m)=s\phi(m)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(s\otimes m)=s\phi(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in M(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in M(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that if <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in M(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in M(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=x\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=x\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in R^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(m)=\phi(x)\phi(\epsilon)\in M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(m)=\phi(x)\phi(\epsilon)\in M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks routinely that <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the defining relations in presentation (<a href="#S7.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 7.1. Basic definitions and results ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>). Hence <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> induces a monoid homomorphism <math id="S7.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\to M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\to M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">First we show that <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> surjective. For any <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the element of <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> whose <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th component is <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and whose other components are <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\in S^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\dots,\beta_{n}\in S^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly. Let now <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in S^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in S^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=y\phi(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=y\phi(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=y\phi(\epsilon)=\sum_{k=1}^{n}y_{k}\beta_{k}\phi(\epsilon)=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\eta(y_{k}\otimes\alpha_{k}\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=y\phi(\epsilon)=\sum_{k=1}^{n}y_{k}\beta_{k}\phi(\epsilon)=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\eta(y_{k}\otimes\alpha_{k}\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S7.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we show that <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. Suppose that <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(s\otimes m)=\eta(s^{\prime}\otimes m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(s\otimes m)=\eta(s^{\prime}\otimes m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\phi(m)=s^{\prime}\phi(m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\phi(m)=s^{\prime}\phi(m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\phi(m_{k})=s^{\prime}\phi(m^{\prime}_{k})~(1\leq k\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\phi(m_{k})=s^{\prime}\phi(m^{\prime}_{k})~(1\leq k\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S7.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S7.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

