<div id="S7.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.4</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:R\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:R\to S</annotation></semantics></math> be a homomorphism of <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded rings and <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> an idempotent matrix with homogeneous entries such <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\cong M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\cong M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> as graded <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-modules, where <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\epsilon)\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\epsilon)\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by applying <math id="S7.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to each entry.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of the previous lemma shows that there is an isomorphism <math id="S7.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\to M(\phi(\epsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:S\otimes_{R}M(\epsilon)\to M(\phi(\epsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. We leave it to the reader to check that <math id="S7.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the grading.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
