<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.6</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid isomorphism <math id="S7.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big\langle[P]=[Q]\big\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big\langle[P]=[Q]\big\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> given by tensoring.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 7.5. ‣ 7.2. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra I ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a> there is a monoid isomorphism <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> given by tensoring. Clearly the monoid congruence on <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the relations <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid congruence. It follows that <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid since <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid. Since tensoring preserves the action of <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism of <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoids. Clearly the relation <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P]=[Q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P]=[Q]</annotation></semantics></math> generates the same <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid congruence on <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> as the relations <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)=\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P]=[Q]\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)=\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P]=[Q]\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7.7</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the Leavitt algebra <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k)</annotation></semantics></math>. As already observed by Bergman <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>,</p>
<table id="S7.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k)\cong\mathsf{k}\langle h,h^{-1}:\overline{\mathsf{k}^{n}}\cong\overline{\mathsf{k}^{n+k}}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>𝗄</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>𝗄</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>≅</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>𝗄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k)\cong\mathsf{k}\langle h,h^{-1}:\overline{\mathsf{k}^{n}}\cong\overline{\mathsf{k}^{n+k}}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Theorem 5.2]</cite></p>
<table id="S7.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k))\cong\mathcal{V}(\mathsf{k})/\langle[\mathsf{k}^{n}]=[\mathsf{k}^{n+k}]\rangle\cong M_{n,n+k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝗄</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝗄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(L_{\mathsf{k}}(n,n+k))\cong\mathcal{V}(\mathsf{k})/\langle[\mathsf{k}^{n}]=[\mathsf{k}^{n+k}]\rangle\cong M_{n,n+k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, for <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,k\in\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,k\in\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n,n+k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n,n+k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the finite commutative monoid</p>
<table id="S7.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n,n+k}:=\big\{0,x,2x,\dots,nx,\dots,(n+k-1)x\big\},\ \ \ \ \mbox{with relation}\ (n+k)x=nx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with relation</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n,n+k}:=\big\{0,x,2x,\dots,nx,\dots,(n+k-1)x\big\},\ \ \ \ \mbox{with relation}\ (n+k)x=nx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
