<div id="S7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 7.1 ([, Proposition 66]). ‣ 7.1. Basic definitions and results ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm9" title="Theorem 6.9. ‣ 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Theorem 5.1]</cite> and <a href="#S6.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 6.10. ‣ 6.2. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras II ‣ 6. Smash products of graded Bergman algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a> that</span></p>
