<p id="S7.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to show that the isomorphism <math id="S7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\big\langle[P_{1}^{(\gamma)}],[P_{2}^{(\gamma)}]~(\gamma\in A)\mid[P(\gamma)]=[P_{1}^{(\gamma)}]+[P_{2}^{(\gamma)}]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big\rangle\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\big\langle[P_{1}^{(\gamma)}],[P_{2}^{(\gamma)}]~(\gamma\in A)\mid[P(\gamma)]=[P_{1}^{(\gamma)}]+[P_{2}^{(\gamma)}]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big\rangle\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by tensoring. But that follows from Lemmas <a href="#S7.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7.1. Basic definitions and results ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, <a href="#S7.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 7.3. ‣ 7.1. Basic definitions and results ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a> and <a href="#S7.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 7.4. ‣ 7.1. Basic definitions and results ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a>, see the proof of Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 7.5. ‣ 7.2. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra I ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
