<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>Realisation of <math id="S8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoids as non-stable <math id="S8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-theory of graded rings</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section, <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is an abelian group, <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded field concentrated in degree zero, and <math id="S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded <math id="S8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra. Recall from §<a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. Γ-monoids ‣ 2. Γ-monoids and graded algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> that if <math id="S8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M,i)</annotation></semantics></math> is a pointed <math id="S8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid with <math id="S8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in M</annotation></semantics></math> an <math id="S8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-order unit, then <math id="S8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a strong order unit if for any <math id="S8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq ki" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq ki</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, <math id="S8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is an invariant order unit if <math id="S8.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\gamma}i=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>i</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\gamma}i=i</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S8.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8.1</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M,i)</annotation></semantics></math> be a pointed conical <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid with a distinguished order unit <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a hereditary graded <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:(M,i)\cong(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R),[R])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:(M,i)\cong(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R),[R])</annotation></semantics></math> as pointed <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoids. Furthermore, <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> has a weak universal property: if <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra with <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid homomorphism <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:(M,i)\rightarrow(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S),[S])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:(M,i)\rightarrow(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S),[S])</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is a (nonunique) graded <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following diagram commutes.</span></p>
