<div id="S8.Thmthm1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore,</span></p>
<ol id="S8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a strongly graded ring if and only if
</span><math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a strong order unit.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a crossed-product ring if and only if </span><math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an invariant order unit.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X=\{i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}\mid\phi\in\Phi\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}\mid\phi\in\Phi\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of non-zero generators for the <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid <math id="S8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each <math id="S8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> there are <math id="S8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\phi,1},\dots,\gamma_{\phi,n_{\phi}}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\phi,1},\dots,\gamma_{\phi,n_{\phi}}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}+q_{\phi}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></munderover><mmultiscripts><mi>i</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}+q_{\phi}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=\{u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}\mid\psi\in\Psi\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=\{u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}\mid\psi\in\Psi\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of relations, including the relations (<a href="#S8.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 8. Realisation of Γ-monoids as non-stable 𝐾-theory of graded rings ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.1</span></a>), such that <math id="S8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\langle X\mid Y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\langle X\mid Y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is conical, we may assume that <math id="S8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\psi},v_{\psi}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\psi},v_{\psi}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all pairs <math id="S8.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite subset of <math id="S8.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite subset of <math id="S8.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ol id="S8.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(I)</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">in the relations <math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}~(\psi\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}~(\psi\in B)</annotation></semantics></math> only the generators <math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}~(\phi\in A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}~(\phi\in A)</annotation></semantics></math> appear,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(II)</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the relations <math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}~(\psi\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}~(\psi\in B)</annotation></semantics></math> include the relations <math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}+q_{\phi}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}i~(\phi\in A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>i</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}+q_{\phi}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}i~(\phi\in A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define a partial order <math id="S8.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S8.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S8.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S8.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subseteq B^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subseteq B^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly <math id="S8.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,\leq)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,\leq)</annotation></semantics></math> is a directed set. For any <math id="S8.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\in Z</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="S8.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{(A,B)}=\langle X_{(A,B)}\mid Y_{(A,B)}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{(A,B)}=\langle X_{(A,B)}\mid Y_{(A,B)}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.p2.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{(A,B)}=\{i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}\mid\phi\in A\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(A,B)}=\{i,p_{\phi},q_{\phi}\mid\phi\in A\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{(A,B)}=\{u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}\mid\psi\in B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{(A,B)}=\{u_{\psi}=v_{\psi}\mid\psi\in B\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S8.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, then clearly there is a canonical <math id="S8.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid homomorphism <math id="S8.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{(A,B)}^{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}:M_{(A,B)}\to M_{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{(A,B)}^{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}:M_{(A,B)}\to M_{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks easily that <math id="S8.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct limit of the direct system <math id="S8.p2.m31" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{M_{(A,B)},\alpha_{(A,B)}^{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}\mid(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})\in Z\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{(A,B)},\alpha_{(A,B)}^{(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})}\mid(A,B)\leq(A^{\prime},B^{\prime})\in Z\}</annotation></semantics></math> in the category of <math id="S8.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoids.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now fix an <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\in Z</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}_{(A,B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}_{(A,B)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra obtained from <math id="S8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by adjoining idempotent endomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
