</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a limit ordinal and <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has been defined for all <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the
direct limit of <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{\alpha})_{\alpha&lt;\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{\alpha})_{\alpha&lt;\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, Theorem 3.4]</cite> the algebra <math id="S8.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is hereditary. Now choose an ordinal <math id="S8.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and a bijection <math id="S8.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to\psi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to\psi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S8.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S8.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>. We build graded <math id="S8.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras <math id="S8.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S8.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</span></p>
<ol id="S8.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="S8.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Start with the algebra <math id="S8.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed above.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(e)</span> 
<div id="S8.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha+1}</annotation></semantics></math> be obtained from <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> by adjoining an isomorphism <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{U_{\psi_{\alpha}}}\cong\overline{V_{\psi_{\alpha}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>≅</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{U_{\psi_{\alpha}}}\cong\overline{V_{\psi_{\alpha}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\psi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\psi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\psi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\psi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the graded <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules corresponding to <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\psi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\psi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.I4.i5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\psi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\psi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(f)</span> 
<div id="S8.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S8.I4.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> is a limit ordinal and <math id="S8.I4.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has been defined for all <math id="S8.I4.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="S8.I4.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the
direct limit of <math id="S8.I4.i6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{\alpha})_{\lambda\leq\alpha&lt;\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{\alpha})_{\lambda\leq\alpha&lt;\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, Theorem 3.4]</cite> the algebra <math id="S8.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is hereditary. Clearly <math id="S8.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mu}\cong R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mu}\cong R</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to prove the weak universality of the <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose that <math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra with <math id="S8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid homomorphism <math id="S8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:(M,i)\rightarrow(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S),[S])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:(M,i)\rightarrow(\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S),[S])</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the following diagram, which gives a <math id="S8.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-monoid homomorphism, <math id="S8.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{(A,B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{(A,B)}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S8.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\in Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
