<div id="S8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{(A,B)}\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R_{(A,B)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{(A,B)}\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R_{(A,B)})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{(A,B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{(A,B)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the universal ring such that
<math id="S8.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{P_{\phi}}\oplus\overline{Q_{\phi}}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}I~(\phi\in A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⊕</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>I</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{P_{\phi}}\oplus\overline{Q_{\phi}}=\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\phi}}{}^{\gamma_{\phi,k}}I~(\phi\in A)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{U_{\psi}}\cong\overline{V_{\psi}}~(\psi\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{U_{\psi}}\cong\overline{V_{\psi}}~(\psi\in B)</annotation></semantics></math> and the images of these modules in <math id="S8.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> give the same relations, it follows that there is a <math id="S8.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-graded homomorphism <math id="S8.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{(A,B)}\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{(A,B)}\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> which induces
<math id="S8.p7.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{(A,B)}=-\otimes_{R_{(A,B)}}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{(A,B)}=-\otimes_{R_{(A,B)}}S</annotation></semantics></math> on the level of monoids. Since the direct limit of <math id="S8.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{(A,B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{(A,B)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,B)\in Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\in Z</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S8.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with direct limits,</span></p>
