<p id="S8.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain that <math id="S8.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\psi_{1}}:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\rightarrow\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\psi_{1}}:\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\rightarrow\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="S8.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> in Diagram <a href="#S8.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 8. Realisation of Γ-monoids as non-stable 𝐾-theory of graded rings ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.2</span></a>.</span></p>
