<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\cong\big\langle v(i)\mid v\in E^{0},\,i\in\mathbb{Z}\big\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)\cong\big\langle v(i)\mid v\in E^{0},\,i\in\mathbb{Z}\big\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">with the <math id="S9.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>-action <math id="S9.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{n}v(i)=v(i+n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>v</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{n}v(i)=v(i+n)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S9.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,i\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,i\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote <math id="S9.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S9.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graded finitely generated projective <math id="S9.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module with <math id="S9.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{k}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗄</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{k}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> appears in <math id="S9.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="S9.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and zero elsewhere. Throughout, we write <math id="S9.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S9.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S9.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{v\in E^{0}}p_{v}\cong R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{v\in E^{0}}p_{v}\cong R</annotation></semantics></math> as graded <math id="S9.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module and the isomorphism classes <math id="S9.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p_{v}(i)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p_{v}(i)]</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to <math id="S9.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(i)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S9.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 9. Application to graph algebras ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.2</span></a>). Next we consider the pairs of graded finitely generated projective <math id="S9.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules
<math id="S9.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{e\in s^{-1}(v)}p_{r(e)}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S9.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in E^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in E^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> that are not sinks. We construct the graded ring</span></p>
