<div id="S9.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, by Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 7.5. ‣ 7.2. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra I ‣ 7. The graded 𝒱-monoid of a graded Bergman algebra ‣ Bergman algebrasThe graded universal algebra constructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>, the monoid <math id="S9.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(L_{\mathsf{k}}(E))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝗄</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(L_{\mathsf{k}}(E))</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by <math id="S9.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>gr</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> subject to relations</span></p>
